  "id": "COMPOUND:18043 - PROTEIN:5856",
  "verbalization": "Arjunglucoside I is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SNU-387 through a series of target relationships. The evidence suggests that Arjunglucoside I acts as a target for Hepatocyte, which in turn is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and Thelephantin K. Both of these compounds have a shared target of SNU-387, indicating a potential convergent pathway. Additionally, Arjunglucoside I is also linked to Raji, which is targeted by 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, dl-, further reinforcing the involvement of this compound in a broader network of interactions. The integration of these pathways suggests that Arjunglucoside I may exert its biological effects through a mechanism that ultimately influences SNU-387, possibly through the modulation of metabolic or signaling pathways in hepatocytes. The evidence supports a role for Arjunglucoside I in the regulation of SNU-387, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
